# Swift tests

Follow the project skill `.agents/skills/add-swift-test/SKILL.md`.

- Files live in `macos/ProvenenciaTests/`, not next to app sources. Swift Testing (`@Test`, `#expect`), `@testable import Provenencia`.
- Inject `FakeStore` and temp `OnboardingFolders`. No `GoStore`, dylib, or generated protobuf tests.
- `@MainActor` when exercising `OnboardingModel`. Wire new files into the ProvenenciaTests target in `project.pbxproj` only.

```swift
@Test func loadWithNoIdentityShowsChooseFileUnlocked() async throws {
    let (model, _, _) = try harness()
    await model.load()
    #expect(model.phase == .chooseFile)
    #expect(!model.researcherLocked)
}
```
- `FakeStore` seeds rows and scripts `nextWriteEffects`, matching `…Error` hooks, `unlinkImpactBlocks`, and `deleteImpactByID`. It also seeds what Go composes (`seededEventSummaries`, `seededPlaceSummaries`, `seededConclusionDetails`, `eventTitlesByGraph`) without re-implementing reconciliation, graph walks, or the naming matrix. It does not re-implement graph list order, Citation graph membership, WriteEffects composition, or graph / Copy Source refusals — those live in Go. New FakeStore methods follow the same scripting shape and add none of those rules; leftover synthesizers, vocabulary `CoreInvokeError`s, and local sorts outside that set are not the pattern to copy. Test engine rules in Go.
